  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Episc">Episc</ref> 4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-q">operari cum seculi iudicibus, qui rectum uelle diligunt,</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-x">He sceall georne saca sehtan ⁊ frið wyrcan mid þam woruld-deman, þe riht lufian.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-x">He sceall georne saca sehtan and frið wyrcan mid þam worulddeman þe riht lufian.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-x">He must readily resolve disputes and make peace along with those secular judges who love justice.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Er soll mit den weltlichen Richtern, die Recht lieben, ernstlich Streitsachen beilegen und Frieden wirken.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">He shall earnestly settle disputes and make peace together with the secular judges who love justice.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="477"><ref target="clause:Episc_9">Episc 9</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">s. u. 9</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:Episc_9">Episc 9</ref>; <ref target="clause:Episc_12">Episc 12</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares 9.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">resolve disputes: The bishop’s role in secular dispute resolution had been established in English law at least as early as 2–3 Edgar.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
